# Normalize line endings on checkout so text content is byte-identical
# across platforms. windows-latest GitHub Actions runners ship with
# core.autocrlf=true by default, which otherwise rewrites LF to CRLF for
# any file git treats as text - silently breaking exact byte/string
# comparisons in tests.
* text=auto eol=lf

# testdata/corpus/*.csv fixtures are compared byte-for-byte in
# corpus_test.go (a leading UTF-8 BOM, an embedded newline inside a
# quoted field, exact delimiters). Mark them binary so git never
# reinterprets or converts them, regardless of platform or a
# contributor's local core.autocrlf setting.
testdata/corpus/*.csv -text
